{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.ProlongedPeriodsFixedDepth","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.ProlongedPeriodsFixedDepth","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.End","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Card"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.prolongation_fixed_depth_recurrence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.prolongation_fixed_depth_recurrence","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/prolonged-periods-fixed-depth.lean#L35-L47","doc":"**Existence half of the keystone.** If the prolongation operator `M`\nsatisfies the depth-`d` polynomial relation `M^d = Σ_{j<d} c_j • M^j`\n(Cayley–Hamilton on the finite-rank period space), then its powers obey the\ndepth-`d` linear recurrence `M^{n+d} = Σ_{j<d} c_j • M^{n+j}` for every `n`,\nwith the SAME `n`-independent kernel. Hence so does every period orbit. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:prolonged-periods-fixed-depth","label":"prop:prolonged-periods-fixed-depth","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/prolonged-periods-fixed-depth.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}